      "output": "3"
    },
    {
      "input": "citations = [1, 3, 1]",
      "output": "1"
    },
    {
      "input": "citations = [0]",
      "output": "0"
    }
  ],
  "signature": {
    "method": "hIndex",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "citations",
        "type": "int[]"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int"
  },
  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public int hIndex(int[] citations) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "The answer can't be more than the number of papers.",
    "Bucket papers by citation count (capping at n), then walk from high to low accumulating counts.",
    "buckets = [0]*(n+1)\nfor c in citations: buckets[min(c, n)] += 1\ntotal = 0\nfor h from n down to 0:\n    total += buckets[h]\n    if total >= h: return h",
    "Counting sort makes this O(n); sorting descending and finding the last `citations[i] >= i + 1` is O(n log n)."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
